"note":null},{"event_row_id":"262537","hazard":"tornado","ncei_type":"Tornado","place":"QN","begin":"2010-09-16 16:42:00","end":"2010-09-16 16:46:00","deaths_direct":{"v":1,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"injuries_direct":{"v":1,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"damage_property":{"v":17200000,"s":"ok","u":"$","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"magnitude":null,"magnitude_type":null,"flood_cause":null,"tor_scale":"EF1","report_source":"NWS Storm Survey","event_narrative":"A National Weather Service Storm Survey Team confirmed a tornado in Queens.||The tornado impacted Flushing and Bayside.  In Flushing, on Browne Street between Roosevelt and 38th Avenues, the third floor of a residential brick building was severely damaged structurally.  Large tree tops were lying on top of buildings and shot like projectiles between buildings.  Sides of houses were peeled back.  There was clear evidence of twisted metal along the side of the building.  On Warren Street near the intersection of Roosevelt Avenue, a steel framed water tower was blown over on the roof.  There was a partial roof collapse on another residential building.||A Pennsylvania woman was killed in her car by a falling tree on Grand Central Parkway.  Her passenger was injured.  A man trying to assist the woman suffered a brain aneurysm and died. ||The tornado touched down around 2.5 miles south of Flushing and lifted 1 mile northeast of Bayside over Little Neck Bay.","lat":40.74,"lon":-73.84,"note":null},{"event_row_id":"262507","hazard":"thunderstorm","ncei_type":"Thunderstorm Wind","place":"QN","begin":"2010-09-16 16:42:00","end":"2010-09-16 16:42:00","deaths_direct":{"v":0,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"injuries_direct":{"v":0,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"damage_property":{"v":null,"s":"missing","u":"$","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"magnitude":"61.00","magnitude_type":"EG","flood_cause":null,"tor_scale":null,"report_source":"Public","event_narrative":"Trees were down on 75th Street and 37th Avenue, 